      "pages": null,
      "notes": "Rule R5: \"In conformance with the ISCII standard, the half-consonant form RRA h is represented as eyelash-RA. This form of RA is commonly used in writing Marathi and Newari.\" Table 12-8 note: \"Marathi also makes use of the eyelash form of the letter RA, as discussed in rule R5.\" Used here for the three letters with no attested use in this language: each reads as its base letter."
